   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Extremely poor and poor households benefiting from Bonoluz</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2020-01-09" value="330000" year="2020"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-09"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-09"></period-end>
     <target value="900000">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mostly Achieved. The ambitious target was maintained in the context of the expanion of social program as a result of the general price hike even though tariff increases were suspended. Throughout 2023 and 2024, prices stablized leaving less need to maintain the same level of social transfers to the poorest households.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="539040"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reduction from baseline of energy use in public buildings</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2022-01-09" value="0" year="2022"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-09"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-09"></period-end>
     <target value="2">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Not Achieved. This derived from the data of EDEs and was shared by MEM, which monitors this on a regular basis. The Government has not yet launched investment projects to improve energy efficiency in its buildings. A number of energy audits have been carried out and a comprehensive investment program covering more than 1,500 buildings has been prepared but the GoDR has not yet decided to seek the needed financing.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="-5"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">New renewable energy capacity consistent with least-cost planning and contracted through competitive procurement by distribution companies</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2022-01-09" value="0" year="2022"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-09"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-09"></period-end>
     <target value="500">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Not Achieved. Prior to the President&apos;s issuance of the Decree mandating the competitive procurement of renewable energy (RE) (PA4(i), approximately 2,500 MW of RE capacity had already been agreed upon and approved through bilateral negotiations. Of this capacity, 179 MW of power purchase agreements (PPAs) were signed in 2022, and an additional 1,180 MW in 2023. The implementation of these agreements have contributed to delays in the initiation of a competitive procurement process for new RE capacity. The GoDR is preparing plans for such a process, but no RE has been contracted through competitive procurement.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="0"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Distribution companies that have signed performance agreements with CUED including a publicly disclosed list of KPIs and published annual audited financial statements for calendar years 2020 to 2023</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2022-01-09" value="0" year="2022"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-09"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-09"></period-end>
     <target value="3">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partially Achieved. The EDEs signed performance agreements with CUED including a publicly disclosed list of KPIs. The audited financial statements for 2020 for the three EDEs were published on their respective websites. The audits for the financial statements for 2021-2023 are to be delivered at the end of 2025.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="1.5"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Distribution companies with all key management positions filled following competitive procurement using meritocratic criteria by 2024</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2022-01-09" value="0" year="2022"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-09"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-09"></period-end>
     <target value="3">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Achieved. By December 2024, the indicator was achieved, with all three CEOs selected. Two were on board before the end of the year, while the appointment of the final CEO officially took effect in February 2025, completing the transition to 100 percent technical leadership (moving away from the previous practice of political appointees).</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="3"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Distribution companies that have data collection systems in place allowing them to effectively monitor progress on Key Performance Indicators</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2022-01-09" value="0" year="2022"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-09"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-09"></period-end>
     <target value="3">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Exceeded. The three EDEs have the data collection systems in place allowing them to effectively monitor progress on Key Performance Indicators. The systems include technologies like Power BI and SAP, which allows them to visualize the data in different ways. The EDEs are effectively using these systems to monitor their commercial and operational performance and regularly report on the KPIs.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="3"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
